    drm/panel: Add LG Fx0 JDI in-cell panel support
    
    Translate production revision initialization, touch-countermeasure
    commands and reset/bias sequencing from the LG madai kernel. Preserve
    boot GPIO state at probe and prepare the DSI host before resetting the
    panel. Use a non-continuous clock lane so it can enter LP11. Send DCS
    display-off and sleep-in from disable(), before video shutdown.
    
    Track the VDD enable reference and rejected cleanup. Return power-off
    errors to the panel core and finish pending cleanup before acquiring
    another reference. The earlier proposal ignored these errors, allowing a
    hardware-disable rejection before consumer decrement to leave a supply
    reference behind while DRM considered the panel unprepared. Attempt all
    rail shutdown steps and report the first error.
    
    Adapt Timothy Schmidt's original local driver proposal
    a22c81819da3102002a0975091245e8347723be1 and fold its later local changes
    51190c24d336111f84835fa7f30603aafd856e5f and
    9723635946c45921e78e4e03c32eb1c29ca7f574 into this introduction. Retain
    original authorship, date and vendor copyrights. Codex (GPT-6) assisted
    with adaptation, cleanup tracking and qualification. These local fixes
    are folded into the new feature rather than proposed as mainline fixes.
    
    Native Qualcomm ARM built-in and ARM64 module profiles compile this
    panel and the DRM panel/DSI cores with W=1 and no warnings. Extracted
    panel and current DRM/regulator code passes 16 modeled power cases;
    the earlier proposal fails eight and both cleanup regressions are
    rejected. Actual on/off callbacks and DRM multi helpers match vendor
    production payloads and waits in 18 command/error cases; three command,
    wait and order regressions are rejected. Hardware I/O is mocked.
    
    Late regulator failures after consumer decrement, coupled supplies,
    physical sequencing and recovery are unqualified. Historical testing
    removed a DCS-off timeout but still reset during later host/PLL shutdown;
    this proposal does not establish complete cycling. Human review of the
    proposed maintainer entry and DCO certification remain pending.

